{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_13-51-31-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\n \\\"rationale\\\": (\\\"The revised identity probe produced a receipt without parse loss, so the third finding moves from explained to a citation-backed holds, and the behavior behind it is promoted as durable knowledge.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\": (\\\"drain_notifiers resolves a pending append_notify by index coverage before it considers leadership: for a pending call with a recorded assignment \"'`(idx, ballot)` the arm `Some((idx, _)) if idx <= decided` is matched before \"\n   \"`Some((idx, ballot)) if ballot < cur_ballot`, so once the node'\"'s decided index reaches idx the call resolves Ok(idx) without establishing that the entry at idx is the entry the call submitted. The ballot-based Superseded arm therefore \\\"\n   \\\"only fires while decided < idx; with a current ballot the call would otherwise have to time out. In the probed construction node 1's own entry was accepted at index 1 and never replicated, node 2 was elected with an empty log and decided \\\"\n   \\\"index 1 with its own entry, and after node 1 re-synchronized (Promise + AcceptSync truncating its log to node 2's) node 1's call resolved Ok(1) while the entry at index 1 was node 2's, not node 1's.\\\"),\n  \\\"conditions\\\": (\\\"omnipaxos_runtime actor; the caller's entry was assigned an index but was not adopted by the following leader (e.g. it never reached a quorum), the node then re-synchronizes with that leader so its decided index covers the assigned \\\"\n   \\\"index with a different entry, and the call's deadline has not yet passed.\\\"),\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_drain_notifiers_timeout\\\",\\\"src_append_notify_contract\\\",\\\"src_superseded_doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"743518e2b7a040ad9272d821ba327ef3\\\":[1]},\n }],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"dcb373d7a7c843d981030cdf4ec8d37a-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"5ae5e40c713c4c6488aa865e7a16ef53-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_drain_notifiers_timeout\\\",\\\"src_append_notify_contract\\\",\\\"src_superseded_doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"743518e2b7a040ad9272d821ba327ef3\\\":[1,0]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"holds\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\": (\\\"Current account. Source: drain_notifiers matches a pending call's recorded assignment in the order \"'`Some((idx, _)) if idx <= decided` first and `Some((idx, ballot)) if ballot < cur_ballot` second (actor.rs:201-222), so \"\n   \"index coverage alone resolves the call Ok(idx), without establishing that the entry at idx is the one the call submitted; the Superseded arm exists for the leadership-change case and its own documentation concedes the entry may never be \"\n   \"decided (event.rs:45-60), while the Ok contract is to await the entry'\"'s decided log index (handle.rs:114-137). Execution 743518e2b7a040ad9272d821ba327ef3 (experiment 5ae5e40c713c4c6488aa865e7a16ef53-experiment, exit 0, its single \\\"\n   \\\"test passed, parsing_error_count 0) parsed both events of the construction: event 1 \"'`overwritten_index_resolution` {a_decided_idx: 1, a_entry_at_index_1_is_own: false, b_decided_idx: 1, b_idx: 1, resolution: '\"\\\\\\\"Ok(1)\\\\\\\"} and event 0 \\\"\n   \\\"\"'`after_b_takeover` {b_leader: '\"\\\\\\\"2:true\\\\\\\", c_leader: \\\\\\\"2:true\\\\\\\", a_leader: \\\\\\\"1:true\\\\\\\", b_decided: 0, c_decided: 0}. Read together: at the moment node 2 was the leader (observed by nodes 2 and 3) and had decided nothing, node 1 still \\\"\n   \\\"believed itself leader (a_leader 1:true) and held its own entry at index 1; node 2's own call was assigned index 1 (b_idx 1) and decided it (b_decided_idx 1); after node 1's reconnect re-synchronized it, node 1's decided index was 1 and \\\"\n   \\\"the entry there was not its own (a_entry_at_index_1_is_own false), yet its call resolved Ok(1). So the declared comparison holds: the completion endpoint reported success at the very index whose decided entry is a different entry, and the \\\"\n   \\\"Superseded heuristic never fired because the index-based arm is matched first. Premises the construction supplies rather than assumes: node 1 really held its own entry at index 1 before the sync (read back as Undecided) and node 2's log was \\\"\n   \\\"empty at takeover because node 1 was isolated in both directions. Counter-limitations kept in force: (a) the interleaving is constructed deliberately and its frequency in a deployment is not measured; (b) the call is only misleading if \\\"\n   \\\"Ok(idx) is read as 'the submitted entry is decided at idx', which is what the handle documentation and the crate's own usage example state ('durably decided at log idx'); the actor cannot compare entry values (Entry is only Clone + Debug), so \\\"\n   \\\"an honest fix would have to key on the assignment's ballot (e.g. report Superseded whenever it is no longer current) instead of comparing entries; (c) the case requires the assigned entry not to be adopted and a leader change before the \\\"\n   \\\"call's deadline.\\\"),\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The overwritten-index interleaving is constructed deliberately; nothing is claimed about how likely it is in a deployment.\\\",\n   \\\"Whether Ok(idx) must mean 'the submitted entry is decided at idx' is a contract reading: the handle documentation and the crate's example say so ('durably decided at log idx'), but Entry is only Clone + Debug so the actor cannot verify identity by comparing values.\\\",\n   \\\"The probe uses a 2-second tick period and a 5-second per-call deadline so that the resolution tick cannot land between node 1's promise change and its re-synchronization; the same case at other cadences is not measured.\\\"]\n }]\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
