{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The identity finding is now citation-backed. Receipt 743518e2b7a040ad9272d821ba327ef3 (experiment 5ae5e40c713c4c6488aa865e7a16ef53-experiment, exit 0, its single test passed, parsing_error_count 0) parsed both events: index 1 `overwritten_index_resolution` {a_decided_idx:1, a_entry_at_index_1_is_own:false, b_decided_idx:1, b_idx:1, resolution:\\\"Ok(1)\\\"} and index 0 `after_b_takeover` {b_leader:\\\"2:true\\\", c_leader:\\\"2:true\\\", a_leader:\\\"1:true\\\", b_decided:0, c_decided:0} — read together, node 1's append_notify resolved Ok(1) for its own entry after its index was taken by node 2's entry, while node 1 still believed itself leader and node 2 was the leader with an empty log. The question moves to holds with defect_claim asserted, the remaining premises of the construction are stated explicitly, and the limits kept: the interleaving is constructed rather than sampled, Ok(idx) means 'the submitted entry is decided at idx' only as a contract reading (Entry is Clone + Debug, so identity cannot be checked by value), and the probe's cadence is 2s ticks with a 5s deadline. A Behavior was also promoted with the clean receipt: the index-coverage arm of drain_notifiers is matched before the ballot-based Superseded arm, so Superseded can only fire while decided < idx. The run now stands on three supported findings — the event-channel park (node- and cluster-level), the core's missing accept-phase repair for a lost Accepted, and this completion-endpoint identity failure. No necessary work is left unfinished; further scope (frequency of the interleaving, wider clusters for the core gap) stays recorded as limits rather than open duties.\"}"}}
